    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nWe categorize angles that are not right, straight, or full into three groups.\n\nContent:\n- An acute angle has a measure between [MATH: 0^\\circ] and [MATH: 90^\\circ\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[IMG: /graphics/da96ee34aafe8dd3f89bff2f146ddcb2]\n- An obtuse angle has a measure between [MATH: 90^\\circ] and [MATH: 180^\\circ\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[IMG: /graphics/4b258aab2483422654b33317693edc24]\n\nContent:\n- Angles whose measure is between [MATH: 180^\\circ] and [MATH: 360^\\circ] are called reflex angles.\n\n[IMG: /graphics/d52887cae6395f2c49e1538ab2f08cb6]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Identifying Acute Angles\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhich of the following shows an acute angle [MATH: \\angle CDE?]\n\n[IMG: /graphics/65fb0d914d66b76ce6f4353343dab1b3]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that an acute angle has a measure between [MATH: 0^\\circ] and [MATH: 90^\\circ.] Therefore, the correct diagram is the following:\n\n[IMG: /graphics/7431adeb0efb3e768acaf628589e15fd]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following shows an acute angle [MATH: \u2220ABC?]\n\nChoices:\na. [IMG: /graphics/q-27025-a-5]\nb. [IMG: /graphics/q-27025-a-1]\nc. [IMG: /graphics/q-27025-a-4]\nd. [IMG: /graphics/q-27025-a-3]\ne. [IMG: /graphics/q-27025-a-2]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following shows an acute angle [MATH: \u2220PQR?]\n\nChoices:\na. [IMG: /graphics/q-115268-a-3]\nb. [IMG: /graphics/q-115268-a-4]\nc. [IMG: /graphics/q-115268-a-5]\nd. [IMG: /graphics/q-115268-a-1]\ne. [IMG: /graphics/q-115268-a-2]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Identifying Obtuse Angles\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhich of the following shows an obtuse angle [MATH: \\angle ABC?]\n\n[IMG: /graphics/b80c3a6e306c0cda325e1d2623e7b619]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that an obtuse angle has a measure between [MATH: 90^\\circ] and [MATH: 180^\\circ.] Therefore, the correct diagram is the following:\n\n[IMG: /graphics/4d9ab01da76704f8f934bb11e32a1ba6]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following shows an obtuse angle [MATH: \u2220ABC?]\n\nChoices:\na. [IMG: /graphics/q-27023-a-5]\nb. [IMG: /graphics/q-27023-a-4]\nc. [IMG: /graphics/q-27023-a-1]\nd. [IMG: /graphics/q-27023-a-2]\ne. [IMG: /graphics/q-27023-a-3]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following shows an obtuse angle [MATH: \u2220PQR?]\n\nChoices:\na. [IMG: /graphics/q-115273-a-5]\nb. [IMG: /graphics/q-115273-a-4]\nc. [IMG: /graphics/q-115273-a-1]\nd. [IMG: /graphics/q-115273-a-2]\ne. [IMG: /graphics/q-115273-a-3]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Identifying Reflex Angles\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhich of the following shows a reflex angle [MATH: \\angle CDE?]\n\n[IMG: /graphics/77367c9f0487bd406a833772d40a7548]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that a reflex angle has a measure between [MATH: 180^\\circ] and [MATH: 360^\\circ.] Therefore, the correct diagram is the following:\n\n[IMG: /graphics/b2291b64d8c813df49922542fc70324f]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following shows a reflex angle [MATH: \u2220ABC?]\n\nChoices:\na. [IMG: /graphics/q-27234-a-3]\nb. [IMG: /graphics/q-27234-a-1]\nc. [IMG: /graphics/q-27234-a-2]\nd. [IMG: /graphics/q-27234-a-4]\ne. [IMG: /graphics/q-27234-a-5]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following shows a reflex angle [MATH: \u2220STU?]\n\nChoices:\na. [IMG: /graphics/q-115605-a-1]\nb. [IMG: /graphics/q-115605-a-2]\nc. [IMG: /graphics/q-115605-a-4]\nd. [IMG: /graphics/q-115605-a-3]\ne. [IMG: /graphics/q-115605-a-5]"
